The US government seized First Republic Bank on May 1st and struck a deal to sell the 

00:00:05.469 --> 00:00:10.449
bulk of its operations to JP Morgan regulators hope the move will head off 

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.880
a chaotic collapse that could reignite the banking crisis.

00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:18.399
Ben Eisen covers banking and finance for the journal.

00:00:18.409 --> 00:00:23.260
He explains how first Republic became the second largest bank to fail in the US and what it 

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.200
means for customers investors and the industry.

00:00:27.649 --> 00:00:32.580
First Republic had this business model that was just sort of been perfectly built for a certain 

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.209
time period when interest rates were really low.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:40.279
Um The bank collected a lot of deposits that made a lot of mortgages but when rates suddenly shifted.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.139
Last year,

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:46.110
the bank's business model started to look a little bit more precarious after 

00:00:46.119 --> 00:00:48.740
Silicon Valley Bank and signature failed.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:49.819
In March,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:54.619
everyone pretty much immediately started looking to first Republic as the next risky bank in the 

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.360
system.

00:00:55.979 --> 00:00:58.189
Silicon Valley Bank and First Republic,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.970
they had similar enough client bases and similar enough risks and 

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:07.790
problems that investors and customers and really anyone in this banking crisis 

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.510
started to kind of lump them together.

00:01:09.809 --> 00:01:14.440
Some of the biggest banks collected $30 billion worth of their own money and they 

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:16.589
deposited it at First Republic Bank,

00:01:16.599 --> 00:01:21.279
basically trying to make up for the deposits that customers had pulled.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.930
It was helpful for a day,

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.529
but it didn't stop the panic coming into April 

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.519
24th versus Republic was already in a pretty bad spot after the bank released its earnings 

